The court, upon receipt of the petition together with the plat and instruments filed therewith, shall submit the same to a special master who shall:
(1) Be an individual who is authorized to practice law in this state;
(2) Be a resident of the judicial circuit of the United States wherein the action is brought;
(3) Be a citizen of this state for not less than three years; and
(4) Have not less than five years of experience litigating or providing opinions on title to land in this state.
